{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>If he says thus.</b> And even though the first condition was that he would take speckled and spotted ones, he did not abide by that, but only one of them did he agree to give him." "<b>Furthermore,</b> the reason for the matter is that this type — streaked — was not mentioned in the first condition, so the wicked man came against him with the claim that these were not Jacob's to take, and he would not acknowledge the truth even from the proof that he took this type. And therefore the first time he removed the streaked from Jacob's portion, and afterward he would negotiate with him of his own will to exchange the speckled ones in Jacob's portion for the streaked ones that were Laban's, cycling back and forth ten times. And the first condition concerning speckled and spotted among the sheep and the goats always stood in its place." "And the verse's saying <b>if he says thus</b> is in the future tense, according to what I explained in the verse's saying ״הֵתֶל בִּי״ — this is precisely correct, for the conduct of the birthing was not based on what he would say at the beginning, but rather on what he was going to say in the end, after the flock's conception. And this was not due to any effort of Jacob's own, but rather it was from HaShem, as he afterward related, that he saw in a dream, etc."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:45:13.894898835Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}